board.com/charts/country-albums/2000-01-01"}, {"title": "www.billboard.com", "url": "https://www.billboard.com/charts/country-albums/2000-12-23"}, {"title": "So Good Together", "url": "https://kiwix.nezernet.duckdns.org/content/wikipedia_ru_all_maxi_2025-06/So_Good_Together"}]}, "The search points to a **platinum** RIAA certification, though I didn't reach the RIAA database directly.\n\n- Wikipedia's article on the album says it was certified platinum by the RIAA. It also reports that the album peaked at number 5 on the Billboard Top Country Albums chart and number 28 on the Billboard 200 with sales of 49,000 copies.\n- Billboard country album chart listings from 2000 mostly show the album with a Platinum RIAA tag. One March 2000 listing shows Gold, and that entry conflicts with the others, so I'd treat it as an outlier or an earlier status.\n- A Wikipedia discography page notes that 27 have received a certification of at least Gold from the Recording Industry Association of America across her albums, but it doesn't list this album's specific award.\n\nTo confirm, check the RIAA's certified-awards database for Reba McEntire's *So Good Together*."], "durationSeconds": 6.010892666, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Y8nPeTqy8VAhuRZGJn5mnH", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
